this week microsoft and tesla announced  major new layoffs joining a growing  number of companies that are cutting  jobs or saying they're going to slow  hiring more than 30 000 layoffs  nationwide in the month of june that's  up nearly 60 percent from a year earlier  and many fear that more layoffs could be  coming amid concerns about a possible  recession linkedin career expert  catherine fisher joins us now with  advice on how to bounce back if you lose  your job catherine thank you for being  here so for those people who have  already lost their job or who are afraid  that in the months ahead they will what  do they do to get their house in order  so you know regardless of the job market  you should always be prepared so the  first thing is you know make sure that  you're tending to your network and what  i mean by that is think about it like  gardening you plant the seeds you don't  just you know  ignore it for three years make sure  you're out there talking to your network  it doesn't mean you have to go out to  dinner every week join the conversations  that they're having participate check in  on people that's really important  because you're going to need to rely on  that community that you've built over  the years to help you if you need a job  and if that calendar notification has  come up and hr wants to see you at 9am  the next day and then you get the little  packets slid across the table yes what  do you do then what do you do well first  it's it's okay to be upset i mean this  is an upsetting time if this happens to  you so take that moment take the the you  know the days that you need to prepare  but when you go out into the job market  make sure that you are positive that  you're really leaning into that network  of yours that you are signaling to  people that you're open to work the good  news is that this stigma has really  changed and there's actually tools on  linkedin to be able to notify recruiters  if you're open to work and if you're  comfortable to your broader network you  can also what we're seeing is people are  sharing this on linkedin so they are  talking about you know i've been laid  off what how can you help me  and i think it's really important that  people start leaning into this wow the  stigma really is changing there is that  image of like the pink slip right but  people are talking about it openly as  they should you know this is just part  of the economy part of life  unfortunately  but for people who you know might be in  a position where you know they were laid  off what industries are hiring right now  right well and this is one thing i do  want to point out is layoffs are  happening but you know hiring is still  happening and so we see you know the  healthcare industry farming forestry  education those industries are hiring  and the south is also having a surge of  hiring so dallas houston's st louis  those places are there's lots of jobs  there um you're so right about the  stigma around layoffs uh i remember i  got laid off in  almost 10 years ago and you get that  little your job has been negatively  impacted thing and i felt a lot of shame  about it you know you feel like oh if  i'd done a better job it would have  worked out differently uh but now people  talk about it online that they're very  open about it are there any guidelines  or things to look out for about being  open about it or just share it all you  know i think what you want to do is be  positive so  what you know try to avoid  lambasting the company that you came  from really be positive and share with  your network what you're looking for so  we um actually you know the we've seen a  lot of people posting this and what's  really wonderful to see in the comments  is people saying hey listen i know of a  job here send me you know i'm going to  message you i'm going to you know  introduce you to this person so being  really clear about what it is that  you're looking for is important to share  and and it is like like i said you  should you know it's okay to be upset  just you want to appear to be  professional do you want to appear  save the real talk for offline yeah it's  like when you're making friends and the  friend of yours gossips about someone  else you're like okay well what are you  saying about me when i'm not here  and that's what employers are looking  for are you seeing a lot of anxiety  right now on linkedin in conversations  because of this yeah you know we  actually did a poll and we asked our  members what what they thought of  layoffs and 37  said that they  were concerned about layoffs 38 said  yeah we think layoffs are coming but  it's not going to happen to me and 22  said no and what was really interesting  though was the conversation happening so  one person pointing out listen it's  these big name companies that have been  doing these layoffs but if you look at  the larger scheme of things it's okay  well thank you so much for all these  tips catherine fisher thanks so much
 

